# Widget Organization

Keep page/screen files focused on composition and state wiring.

- Do **not** declare private widget classes inside page files.
- Do **not** use helper methods that return large or reusable `Widget` trees.
- When a UI section is independent, substantial, or reusable, extract a **public** widget in `presentation/widgets/`.

```text
features/home/presentation/pages/home_page.dart
features/home/presentation/widgets/home_appbar.dart
features/home/presentation/widgets/home_stats_section.dart
```

Widgets should have one responsibility, meaningful names, and data via constructors when possible.

Do not extract a file for every tiny snippet if it hurts navigation. Reuse `lib/core/widgets/` (`AppText`, `AppButton`, `AppCard`, `AppCachedNetworkImage`, etc.) before creating new primitives.
